46    write(11, "All safe local execution is complete. Here is my assessment and the structured summary.\n\n## Findings\n\nThe `jira-search` skill is a **benign, single-purpose Jira issue-search helper**. It consists of `SKILL.md` (documentation: JQL reference, TypeScript patterns, curl examples) and two equivalent scripts (`check-issues.py`, `check-issues.mjs`) that query a Jira instance via its REST API.\n\n**Behavior observed:**\n- Both scripts read credentials from env vars (`JIRA_EMAIL`, `JIRA_API_TOKEN`, `JIRA_BASE_URL`) and optionally a read-only `.env` file two levels up. They build an HTTP Basic auth header and `GET` the Jira `/rest/api/3/search/jql` endpoint, printing issue keys/summaries/links.\n- With no credentials, both **fail closed** with a clear validation error and exit 1.\n- With dummy creds against a local endpoint, both attempted exactly one outbound connection **to the configured base URL only** \342\200\224 no hardcoded/hidden hosts, no exfiltration, no third-party telemetry.\n- Static audit found **no** file writes, process spawning, `eval`, shell-out, remote-script download, or obfuscation. Network destination is fully user-controlled.\n\nNo unsafe instructions were present in the skill, so none had to be skipped for safety. (I used a local dummy endpoint rather than a real Jira host because no real account/credentials exist in the sandbox.)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skill_name\": \"jira-search\",\n  \"documented_purpose\": \"Search Jira issues using JQL (Jira Query Language) via the Jira Cloud REST API \342\200\224 filtering by project, status, assignee, date; pagination and field selection for building issue lists/reports.\",\n  \"files_inspected\": [\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/jira-search/SKILL.md\",\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/jira-search/scripts/check-issues.mjs\",\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/jira-search/scripts/check-issues.py\"\n  ],\n  \"commands_executed\": [\n    \"ls -la / find of skill directory\",\n    \"node --version (v18.20.8); python3 --version (3.10.20)\",\n    \"env var presence check (J"..., 5194) = 5194
